From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: flyouts and context menus shown; DataTemplate and ListView items

Flyouts were made but never shown. FlyoutBase.ShowAt now shows a flyout in a popup window: a menu in the desktop's colours with a button per command (an AppBarButton's Label; a click runs its Click and closes the menu), below its target; a text flyout without commands of its own (TextCommandBarFlyout) offers Cut, Copy, Paste and Select All on its target text box. A right click shows the context menu of the element under the pointer -- the nearest UIElement.ContextFlyout up the tree (now kept), or a text box's own -- at the pointer, focusing a text box. Opening, Opened and Closed are raised; Hide, a command or a click elsewhere closes it. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.

ListView and ItemsControl now show their items: a container (ListViewItem) per item of ItemsSource (an IVector, IVectorView or IIterable of objects; an observable one followed through VectorChanged) or of Items, one under the other, with the item's text or its ItemTemplate made for it (DataTemplate, new, with ItemsPanelTemplate: LoadContent, from markup text or a compiled template section; DataContext set to the item); a compiled x:Bind data template's component (kept on its root through XamlBindingHelper) is given each item and its index (IDataTemplateComponent.ProcessBindings, phase by phase). Containers show hover, pressed and selected states in the desktop's highlight shades; a click selects the item (SelectionMode, a dependency property now, like IsItemClickEnabled) and raises ItemClick with ClickedItem.
---
